# Secrets for the MCP servers, read ONLY by the "mcp" gateway container
# (copy to mcp.env, which is gitignored; the bot never sees this file).
# data/mcp.json refers to them as ${VAR}; a server whose variable is empty is
# skipped (not an error). After a change: docker compose up -d mcp, then /mcp recarregar.
#
# The gateway token itself lives in the main .env (MCP_GATEWAY_TOKEN): compose
# passes just that one value to the gateway.

# GitHub's hosted MCP server: a fine-grained personal access token, read-only
# (Contents, Issues, Pull requests, Metadata: Read) on the repositories you pick.
GITHUB_PAT=
